8}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_multiple_choice.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_multiple_choice-01fffa518acd18fbfc8c461d62c2aa43.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":646,\"h\":768,\"white\":0.88,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.11,\"col\":79}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_multiple_choice_range.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_multiple_choice_range-5ad29614c54f1cc04e74fc4e7f95aedf.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":442,\"h\":366,\"white\":0.94,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.05,\"col\":40}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_nps_range.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_nps_range-19d9e4de2d360c1c36eac73e95788461.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":648,\"h\":384,\"white\":0.76,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.24,\"col\":222}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_numerical.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_numerical-1f6cc7afb0e80fd451753443a9066b1d.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":648,\"h\":358,\"white\":0.79,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.2,\"col\":134}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_numerical_settings.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_numerical_settings-127a1bbf6c3acc1a150f5e3e3b5dbf74.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":542,\"h\":598,\"white\":0.95,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.05,\"col\":32}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_numerical_slider.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_numerical_slider-5ec0ca14f9f692cb7bbeb5531d5b7eb6.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":340,\"white\":0.79,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.2,\"col\":119}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_numerical_slider_settings.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_numerical_slider_settings-b0def7b09acd3dd8e3931c38965c6dfb.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":698,\"h\":748,\"white\":0.95,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.05,\"col\":51}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_order_prioritize.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_order_prioritize-18c67b04590d66924a85841320f04198.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":644,\"h\":944,\"white\":0.9,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.09,\"col\":90}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_order_prioritize_settings.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_order_prioritize_settings-8c7848f566cca1b27250fcc2a0ef9f61.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":656,\"h\":374,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":71}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_phone_number.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_phone_number-4a2db319d23bbaa4343ecbbefa5d8f01.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":646,\"h\":374,\"white\":0.8,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.19,\"col\":169}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_phone_number_settings.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_phone_number_settings-0dd0ac463fe18af74ec2d24be317221f.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":676,\"h\":530,\"white\":0.89,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.11,\"col\":43}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_quick_reply.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_quick_reply-66d717dc627cdef412659bd3e7711178.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":266,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":125}},{\"n\":\"quick_reply.gif\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/quick_reply-bee1d06b99b4ef53bbe901d7fb682e0c.gif\",\"st\":{\"w\":720,\"h\":372,\"white\":0.85,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.15,\"col\":115}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_rating.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_rating-c41b463e9d99b74ab15321b643fa85b8.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":416,\"white\":0.79,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.2,\"col\":104}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_single_choice.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_single_choice-10fad06b0acce5a53dfba32b9f336c69.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":558,\"white\":0.87,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.12,\"col\":38}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_text_input.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_text_input-1a1967edf42a1c8448f9e0833a1d8a97.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":366,\"white\":0.81,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.19,\"col\":67}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_text_input_settings.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_text_input_settings-74cd9168d1d30394b68960c1eaf82ab9.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":524,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":32}},{\"n\":\"data_collection_text_input_rows.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/data_collection_text_input_rows-fdd28b488360c9470a41ca09aefcd9c1.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":650,\"h\":466,\"white\":0.85,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.15,\"col\":37}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/dmn/\",\"len\":5973,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesDecision Table ModuleOn this pageDecision Table Module Introduction​ Define a decision table based on decision rules to read and write BPMN process variables at once. Typical Use Cases​ Example​ In this example, the value of the \\\"app\\\" variable is checked. If it is equal to the string \\\"true\\\", the decision table sets the value \\\"1\\\" in the variable \\\"result\\\". If it is equal to the string \\\"false\\\", the decision table sets the value \\\"2\\\" in the variable \\\"result\\\". Further example​ In the next example, we consider the result of a questionnaire with three questions. From these we want to generate a process variable with the value green, yellow or red. If at least one question was answered with red, the value should also be red. If all questions were answered with green, the value should become green and in the remaining cases the value should become yellow. Since we cannot realize an OR in one line, we create three lines for the case that the output value should become red. We see that the condition in empty cells is automatically considered to be fulfilled. Next, we consider the case where the output value should become green. Since the columns of a row are linked with an AND, it is sufficient if we check the value for green in each cell. After that, it is important that \\\"first\\\" was selected in the rule's settings. This makes it possible that we can map all remaining combinations to the output value yellow. Again, we use that the condition in empty cells is automatically considered to be fulfilled. How to Use the Module​ Input​ By clicking on \\\"Input +\\\" you add another input. The input can be a fixed value, a function, or variable. The value this returns is compared to the rules from top to bottom. If one rule applies the output in the same row is generated. Output​ By clicking on \\\"Output +\\\" you add another output. The output is stored in a variable/key whose name you can choose yourself. Rules​ By clicking on the rule number you can add an annotation, delete it or move the rule up or down. To edit the rule itself you need to click the box and choose an operator and value. Rules settings​ You can choose between \\\"First\\\" and \\\"Rule order\\\" by clicking on \\\"F\\\" / \\\"R\\\". Select \\\"first\\\" if the first matching rule should be applied and \\\"rule order\\\" if every rule should be applied. The default is \\\"first\\\". Useful Tips​ Building a product finder, a skin type test, or something similar has never been easier than with our decision table! You do not have to add every condition to each module. It is much simpler! For this article, you should know how variables work. If you need help with that, read this article first. To use a decision table you need a questionnaire, a decision table, and some outputs. Outputs can be every module you want. The outputs are what the customer will see as a result. In this example, we will build a test on which hobby is best suited for the customer. As a result (outputs) we have swimming, cycling, and jogging. Add a Questionnaire​ First, you add the questions you want to ask. Add at least two questions. For fewer questions, it does not make sense to use a decision table. Then choose the process variables and values for each question and each answer. Pay attention to the correct spelling! Working With the Decision Table​ Now you open the decision table. We need to add as many inputs as you have added questions. Therefore click on “Input +”. Afterwards, add an output by clicking on “Output +”. Next, click on the first field under “Input” and select “process variable”. Fill in the name of the process variable of your first question. In the other field under input, you do the same with the other process variables. Then, click on the field under “Output”, choose “process variable” again, and add a new name. Do not use a name that you have already used. For example, use “skin type” if you are doing a skin type test or use “product” if you are building a product finder. Select 'process specific' for 'Variable scope' if you want the variable to be used only in this agent and 'process independent' if you want the variable to be usable in other agents as well. As a next step, add a new rule. With this, you determine the combinations of your questionnaire. For example, if you have three outputs: jogging, cycling, and swimming, add a rule for every combination after which jogging comes as an output. Because of length, we are showing you how to do it with three combinations. After that, the system will be clear and you can choose more combinations! If the first combination is clicked by the customer the hobby will be cycling. So we add in the fields of the first rule values that fit. The system is similar to the variables at modules. Click on the field under the first input. Choose an operator and add the fitting value. This has to be the value that was set in the first question. Then you add the values in the other fields of your inputs too. Next, you fill in the “Output”. For this, click on the field under hobby. Choose a fixed value and add a name that is fitting. In our case, we will use swimming, jogging, and bicycle. Now the first rule is ready. If this combination is clicked, the customer will get “bicycle” as a result. You need to rule every possibility because otherwise the agent does not know what to send. In that case, there would be no output. tipIf you do not set an “Input”, the row will always match. You can use this as an “else” or “otherwise” row that catches all cases not defined by conditions in the previous rows because it always matches. This should only be done in “First” mode als the last rule. Choose Your Modules​ As the last step, you need to condition your modules. To condition them, click on the small circle of the module. Then choose “hobby” as a process variable in the first field and your output (swimming, jogging, or cycling) as a fixed value in the third field. That's it! Now your chat is customized to the responses of the customer.\",\"alts\":[\"dmn_example.png :: dmn_example_demo\",\"dmn_colour_example.png :: dmn_colour_example_demo\",\"unnamed.png :: Start\",\"answer1.png :: Question\",\"answer2.png :: Question\",\"answer3.png :: Question\",\"input.png :: Add an input\",\"output.png :: Add an output\",\"rules.png :: Add process variables\",\"output_2.png :: Choose outputs\",\"addRules.png :: Add a new rule\",\"rules2.png :: Add rules\",\"rulesReady.png :: Complete rules\",\"fixedValueOutput.png :: Complete output\",\"ready.png :: Add process variables\",\"conditionModules.png :: Condition the modules\",\"conditionReady.png :: Condition is ready\",\"end.png :: Ready\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"dmn_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/dmn_example-405898ce55bed7ad673aa3a7a13196be.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":1076,\"h\":496,\"white\":0.94,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.05,\"col\":42}},{\"n\":\"dmn_colour_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/dmn_colour_example-27df2d69a79b2e35986a082ffbe609d4.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":1402,\"h\":840,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":40}},{\"n\":\"unnamed.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/unnamed-2974af5bae8f28e5b4844446590c7dec.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":208,\"h\":512,\"white\":0.9,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.09,\"col\":122}},{\"n\":\"answer1.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/answer1-3b5784c01d9a75302269ea6c435904ca.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":217,\"h\":512,\"white\":0.92,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.08,\"col\":78}},{\"n\":\"answer2.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/answer2-582ef59c2b21a864af99bd6b3c893357.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":212,\"h\":512,\"white\":0.92,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.08,\"col\":74}},{\"n\":\"answer3.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/answer3-4440158910d486f68679ecc7c6df5709.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":218,\"h\":512,\"white\":0.92,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.08,\"col\":63}},{\"n\":\"input.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/input-d1e61770e2580779c357a3236d114623.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":185,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":105}},{\"n\":\"output.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/output-ecefe95ca940e60f5c3040bde8e19350.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":185,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":109}},{\"n\":\"rules.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/rules-ec4cbf30dc832a308c4c698f350e765c.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":375,\"white\":0.82,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.18,\"col\":103}},{\"n\":\"output_2.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/output_2-be222a168fd42004b8030ea33eefdbdf.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":1920,\"h\":1080,\"white\":0.91,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.09,\"col\":70}},{\"n\":\"addRules.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/addRules-9c14c8317bddc1fe1fb48da42db4d06d.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":196,\"white\":0.91,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.08,\"col\":76}},{\"n\":\"rules2.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/rules2-0716e67d109a9fe533654f51468347b0.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":285,\"white\":0.9,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.1,\"col\":45}},{\"n\":\"rulesReady.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/rulesReady-41a34fb893d354b8b0fd2f04aed135aa.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":273,\"white\":0.93,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.06,\"col\":44}},{\"n\":\"fixedValueOutput.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/fixedValueOutput-c47f2db4121f4e7e558f93806bd12a86.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":247,\"white\":0.88,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.12,\"col\":79}},{\"n\":\"ready.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/ready-7b859c6c49024c7c99eac7d3a12b76e9.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":311,\"white\":0.94,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.06,\"col\":45}},{\"n\":\"conditionModules.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/conditionModules-9e87f0021aff6457b3c43fe56d2e784a.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":276,\"h\":512,\"white\":0.89,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.11,\"col\":205}},{\"n\":\"conditionReady.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/conditionReady-e127cb57f9a317b48f6327f902e4fad7.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":512,\"h\":192,\"white\":0.89,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.11,\"col\":45}},{\"n\":\"end.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/end-5651870c854206cbf34ca9eed1b187ec.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":273,\"h\":512,\"white\":0.76,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.24,\"col\":237}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/email_edit/\",\"len\":539,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesEdit Email Address ModuleOn this pageEdit Email Address Module Introduction​ Allow your customers to edit their email address in the chat. Typical Use Cases​ To keep the email addresses up to date you can use the module Edit email address so that you can stay connected with your customers. How to Use the Module​ Useful Tips​ Allow your customers to edit their email address in the chat. The operation must be confirmed with a code, which is sent to the customer via email. For this step you can define an HTML email template.\",\"alts\":[\"email_edit_example.png :: email_edit_example_demo\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"email_edit_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/email_edit_example-17ceecd18f237a9b5ff58d6705d9af1f.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":644,\"h\":684,\"white\":0.77,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.22,\"col\":103}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/email/\",\"len\":904,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesEmail ModuleOn this pageEmail Module Introduction​ Ask your customers for their email address. Typical Use Cases​ This module goes hand in hand with other modules such as Newsletter-opt in. For a working newsletter subscription process, the email address of the customer must be known. For this e.g. you can place a Email module or Sign-in module above. How to Use the Module​ Useful Tips​ The email is stored in the email variable. You can reuse the value of this variable in texts by using the following expression: ${email}. Ask again for value​ If the variable email already has a value, you can ask the customer again by enabling this option. Terms​ You can add terms that the customer has to accept. While \\\"Do your customers have to agree to terms?\\\" is activated, customers have to accept the terms to enter their email. You can store the terms intern as html file or link to a website.\",\"alts\":[\"email_enter_example.png :: email_enter_example_demo\",\"email_terms_example.png :: email_terms_example_demo\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"email_enter_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/email_enter_example-bb5d67da3283107bc5fea14ff7733bda.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":644,\"h\":430,\"white\":0.83,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.17,\"col\":86}},{\"n\":\"email_terms_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/email_terms_example-e68d9cffd80154dec941d11c13ffd889.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":640,\"h\":434,\"white\":0.81,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.18,\"col\":101}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/email/email_templates/\",\"len\":1394,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesEmail ModuleHow to Add Email HTML Templates in LoyJoyOn this pageHow to Add Email HTML Templates in LoyJoy What This Solution Will Do for You​ There are multiple points where you can configure email templates in LoyJoy. This guide explains how to configure them according to individual preferences. What You Need for This Solution to Work​ Ideally, you would already have an HTML template that you want to enter. If you do not have a template you can create a template in one of these ways: Manually create an HTML template Copy the HTML from one of your existing emails Create an HTML template using a tool such as Canva Add the Template to LoyJoy​ You can add the template to by copying all of the html code to text area in LoyJoy. To check that it's working, you can use the \\\"Preview\\\" button right above the text area. In the template, you can use the ${variable_name} syntax to add variables from LoyJoy to the email that will be sent out. In the preview, the ${variable_name} will be shown as-is, without exchanging the text. Change Images in the Template​ Since the email template is not created by LoyJoy, all images used have to be hosted externally as well. Usually image assets should be hosted on your website. To change an image, you can either change the URL in the HTML template to point to another image. Or you can replace the image you want to change on the server.\",\"alts\":[],\"imgs\":[]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/event/\",\"len\":1414,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesEvent ModuleOn this pageEvent Module Introduction​ Trigger an event with the name of your choice. The event is (1) emitted via LoyJoy JavaScript API, (2) stored in the LoyJoy Analytics database, and (3) triggers Signal process modules that wait for the event name. How to Trigger Custom JavaScript With the Event Module​ The event module can be used to trigger custom JavaScript without using eval(). To do this, you can choose any event name such as trigger_custom_javascript and then listen for this event on your website. To listen for the event, you can use the standard event listeners in JavaScript. Example: document.getElementById('my-widget').addEventListener('event', function (e) { if (e.detail.type === 'trigger_custom_javascript') { console.log('Custom JavaScript event triggered:', e.detail.type); // add your code here }}); This example assumes that the LoyJoy widget has the id my-widget. When the event module triggers an event with the name trigger_custom_javascript, the event listener will execute the custom JavaScript code inside the if statement. We have to check for the event type trigger_custom_javascript because the event listener will receive all events triggered by the LoyJoy widget, and we only want to execute our custom JavaScript for the specific event name. Using this method, we can also use different event names to trigger different custom JavaScript code blocks.\",\"alts\":[],\"imgs\":[]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/external_link/\",\"len\":1798,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesExternal Link ModuleOn this pageExternal Link Module Introduction​ Direct your customers to an external website with a link, seamlessly integrating additional resources and information into your chat interface without disrupting the user agent. Typical Use Cases​ Link external content directly in the chat and customize the appearance in the External Link process module. How to Use the Module​ Link​ Link URL​ Add here the URL for the external link. You can decide if you want to open the website in a new tab or inside the Chat (WebView). If you choose the WebView you have to consider the following. The linked website must not prohibit the integration in an iframe via X-Frame-Options, else the connection will be denied by the web browser. WebView example​ You can activate this option by clicking the settings icon next to the \\\"Link\\\" heading. Trigger event​ You have the chance to trigger an event when the customer clicks on the link. The event is (1) emitted via LoyJoy JavaScript API, (2) stored in the LoyJoyAnalytics database, AND (3) triggers signal BPMN process modules that wait for the event name. You can read about all the events and their function here. You can edit the trigger event using the settings icon next to the Link heading. Appearance​ Embed link content in chat if possible​ Things like YouTube Videos or similar can be shown directly in the chat. When the link content is embedded in the chat, the title and description are no longer displayed. Title​ Add a title that will be shown under the link. Description​ Add a description that will be shown under the link. Alternative to image upload​ An alternative to the usual image upload is to add a process variable in which the URL of the image is stored. This image is then displayed as a new link image.\",\"alts\":[\"external_link_webview_example.png :: external_link_webview_example_demo\",\"external_link_optin.png :: external_link_optin_demo\",\"external_link_description_title.png :: external_link_description_title_demo\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"external_link_webview_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/external_link_webview_example-2ff64b74ad3f03c2b99e7d05c715a9bf.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":690,\"h\":1370,\"white\":0.36,\"black\":0.02,\"mid\":0.62,\"col\":127}},{\"n\":\"external_link_optin.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/external_link_optin-045f1f985b9cfa1325ba4cda213af7c6.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":654,\"h\":424,\"white\":0.84,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.14,\"col\":89}},{\"n\":\"external_link_description_title.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/external_link_description_title-404d3a612be7d79bc3f36aa5160b4c6c.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":654,\"h\":522,\"white\":0.4,\"black\":0.03,\"mid\":0.57,\"col\":534}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/firstname/\",\"len\":826,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesFirst Name ModuleOn this pageFirst Name Module Introduction​ Ask your customer for their first name. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Storage​ If you want to store this information in association with your customer, you must have a sign-in module somewhere before the first name module. If you are not using the sign-in module, you can still use this information in the conversation by using the \\\"firstname\\\" variable with the following syntax: ${firstname} Ask again for value​ If this option is enabled, the customer will be asked again about their first name, even if they have already answered the question. Other texts​ Here you can add an intro and a message which will be sent after the consumer input. Database​ Your customer database has to be activated by LoyJoy to use all the Sign-in functions.\",\"alts\":[\"firstname_example.png :: firstname_example_demo\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"firstname_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/firstname_example-b0434841d8e60cf48a17c770aca58ebe.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":654,\"h\":364,\"white\":0.81,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.18,\"col\":66}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/form/\",\"len\":1442,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesForm ModuleOn this pageForm Module Introduction​ Offer a customizable form to your customers. You can ask for any information you need. The form module is a powerful tool to collect information from your customers. You can ask for their name, email, phone number, address, or any other information you need. You can also ask for multiple pieces of information in one form. How to Use the Module​ Storage​ If you want to store this information in association with your customer, you must have a sign-in module somewhere before the form module. Form Fields​ Start by adding as many form fields as you need. Once a form field is created, define your process variable and scope in which the information should be stored. You can customize the initial value of the form field by entering a source. Next, add a label to guide your customers on what to enter. Fill a description of the form field for AI autocomplete suggestions and validation​ You can fill a description for each form field in natural language. The description will be used for autocomplete suggestions and validation using AI. For example, if you ask for the customer's favorite animal, you can fill the description with \\\"The field should contain the name of an animal like dog, cat or any other animal.\\\". This will help the customer to understand what they should enter and will help to validate the input. Autocomplete will make suggestions bases on the description.\",\"alts\":[],\"imgs\":[]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/gender/\",\"len\":854,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesGender ModuleOn this pageGender Module Introduction​ Ask your customer for their gender. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Storage​ If you want to store this information in association with your customer, you must have a sign-in module somewhere before the gender module. If you are not using the sign-in module, you can still use this information in the conversation by using the \\\"gender\\\" variable with the following syntax: ${gender}. Value​ The value of the gender does not depend on the text you can edit. These are the values: Female: female Male: male Diverse: diverse Other texts​ Here you can add an intro and a message which will be sent after the consumer input. Sign in​ The consumer must be signed in order to save this data. Database​ Your customer database has to be activated by LoyJoy to use all the Sign-in functions.\",\"alts\":[\"gender_example.png :: gender_example_demo\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"gender_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/gender_example-59b88190ea8f7adf6d3f9e3c360b6093.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":654,\"h\":328,\"white\":0.92,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.08,\"col\":186}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/goodbye/\",\"len\":603,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesGoodbye ModuleOn this pageGoodbye Module Introduction​ This module allows you to craft a personalized, professional goodbye message that leaves a positive lasting impression on your customers. By clearly signaling the end of the conversation, you ensure that customers feel acknowledged and valued while understanding that the current interaction has concluded. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Draft your goodbye message Drag the module at the end of your chat flow Put the message into the module Main benefit​ This module is mainly for overview. It behaves like a simple message.\",\"alts\":[\"goodbye_example.png :: goodbye_example_demo\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"goodbye_example.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/goodbye_example-77e339a6050001abc4037de035518f70.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":654,\"h\":110,\"white\":0.97,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.02,\"col\":85}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/handover/\",\"len\":1095,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesHandover via Email ModuleOn this pageHandover via Email Module Introduction​ Let customers get in touch with your team via email. Typical Use Cases​ This module is the perfect solution for support requests, offer consultations and many more! How to Use the Module​ Contact email​ Enter the email address where customer requests will be sent. The core feature is the email, which will be sent to the specified address. The content can be customized using an email template. If no template is provided, a default one will be used. Include variables like ${email} for the customer's address. If the email has been provided beforehand (e.g., via the email module), this field will be pre-filled. Default template​ Additional Contacts / Assignment rules​ Add rules to determine multiple receivers of the request. By using conditions where you specify variables, you are able to connect different requests with different receivers. For cases where no rule applies, the default contact information above is used. Other texts​ Change every text like the placeholders or introduction message.\",\"alts\":[\"intro.gif :: Handover\",\"handover_standard_template.png :: handover_standard_template\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"intro.gif\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/intro-b9ab3a8ba5a815205b07b5045133a35d.gif\",\"st\":{\"w\":352,\"h\":764,\"white\":0.97,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.02,\"col\":98}},{\"n\":\"handover_standard_template.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/handover_standard_template-9e7a345444f21c1197c42c66e243c0e9.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":1232,\"h\":908,\"white\":0.44,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.55,\"col\":64}}]},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/hubspot/\",\"len\":1169,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesHubspot ModuleOn this pageHubspot Module The HubSpot module in LoyJoy supports creating new contacts or updating existing ones in HubSpot. When this module is executed, it checks if a contact with the provided email address exists. If so, it updates the contact; otherwise, it creates a new one. Acquire API-Token​ Create a New App in HubSpot Navigate to your HubSpot account and create a new app. Assign the necessary privileges under the \\\"Scope\\\" tab. For further information refer to the official Hubspot documentation. Properties​ You can retrieve an overview of your contact properties in HubSpot under the contacts section. infoIt is mandatory to map the email property in the Hubspot module. If the email property is not mapped, the module will not work. Furthermore, here is an example for creating properties in LoyJoy. A double opt-in for newsletter subscription can be triggered via Hubspot. The instructions can be seen in this Youtube video or in this Hubspot support article. tipYou can set the contact source in hubspot by using the hs_analytics_source property. You can set pre-defined values like DIRECT_TRAFFIC, PAID_SEARCH, or PAID_SOCIAL.\",\"alts\":[\"create_app.png :: create_app\",\"scope.png :: scope\",\"contacts.png :: contacts\",\"properties.png :: properties\"],\"imgs\":[{\"n\":\"create_app.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/create_app-802be871a47c8366bf0ac455e493d338.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":1924,\"h\":846,\"white\":0.77,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.23,\"col\":109}},{\"n\":\"scope.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/scope-e885581c5a1208684212320256ad5fb6.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":3812,\"h\":1994,\"white\":0.88,\"black\":0.05,\"mid\":0.07,\"col\":85}},{\"n\":\"contacts.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/contacts-df5d0e5075d320ce20f78631fa7d6892.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":3824,\"h\":984,\"white\":0.76,\"black\":0,\"mid\":0.24,\"col\":104}},{\"n\":\"properties.png\",\"s\":\"https://docs.loyjoy.com/assets/images/properties-11549e1d08b1786007d84504b76aa403.png\",\"st\":{\"w\":1106,\"h\":1012,\"white\":0.92,\"black\":0.01,\"mid\":0.08,\"col\":47}}]}]"